ecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Tom Suozzi (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Tom Suozzi, a Democratic incumbent in an even-leaning Long Island district, seeks another term against Republican Mike LiPetri. Raters across the spectrum place the race between Lean Democratic and Safe Democratic, settling on a Likely Democratic consensus, and prediction markets price Suozzi's chances near 87 percent. No public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals and expert judgment.\n\nSuozzi holds a decisive financial edge, with about $5.7 million on hand to LiPetri's $723,000, and has recently added police and firefighter union endorsements. Republicans see an opening: a Trump-linked super PAC has spent roughly $8 million attacking Suozzi over stock trading, and the contest is billed as one of New York's most competitive House races. The district's swing nature and the outside investment keep the outcome from being automatic, but the incumbent starts clearly favored.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9133, "margin": 9.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.894, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8981, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.907, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8709, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8955, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9136, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9155, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9242, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9213, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9012, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8932, "margin": 8.5}]}